IMPORT prelude

-- Land Surveyors Act 1991 (Singapore) -- who may survey, certify, hold out and sue for fees (ss 3, 10), registration (s 12), the
-- practising certificate year (s 15), licensing a limited corporation (s 17(1), (9)), reports of changes (s 19), discipline and its
-- limits (ss 25, 26(6), 27(2), 29), appeal routes (ss 15(10), 16(3), 17(8), 18(4), 28), and the offences (ss 10(5), 30(2), 34).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LSA1991.txt (version in
-- force from 1 October 2025), with amendments to Act 25 of 2024 (wef 1 October 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a surveyor, a surveying
-- firm or a client meets. Not encoded: the Board's constitution and procedure (ss 4-9), certificates of registration (ss 13, 14),
-- licences for unlimited corporations, partnerships and LLPs (s 17(2)-(4)), licence conditions beyond their appeal route (s 18),
-- the Companies Act modifications (s 20), insurance (s 21, rules), Investigation Committees and costs (ss 24, 30(1), 31, 32), fees
-- (s 33), offences by bodies corporate (s 35), immunity (s 36), exemptions (s 37) and rules (s 38). Registered foreign surveyors
-- (s 12A) are defined but s 12A itself is NOT in the deposit (see NOTES.md).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Surveyors Act 1991 -- practice`

DECLARE Who IS ONE OF
    `a registered surveyor with a practising certificate`
    `a registered surveyor without a practising certificate`
    `a suspended registered surveyor`
    `an authorised surveyor`
    `an allied professional`
    `an unregistered person`
    `a licensed corporation`
    `a licensed partnership`
    `a licensed limited liability partnership`
    `a partnership wholly of registered surveyors`
    `an unlicensed corporation`

§§ `3 -- the Government`

-- s 3(1): "Nothing in this Act applies to anything done or omitted to be done by the Government." (2): the Act does not require a
-- public authority supplying survey services under written law "to obtain a licence".
GIVEN `done by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the act` IF NOT `done by the Government`

§§ `10 -- illegal practice`

-- s 25(5): while a suspension order is in force "the person concerned is not for the purposes of this Act to be regarded as having in
-- force a practising certificate".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Who
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a practising certificate in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a registered surveyor with a practising certificate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 10(1): a person must not "certify to the correctness or accuracy of any survey unless the person is an authorised surveyor or a
-- registered surveyor who has in force a practising certificate". (The subsection names only these two; a licensed firm is not among
-- them. Read literally.)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Who
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may certify a survey` IF
        `has a practising certificate in force` `the person`
    OR  CONSIDER `the person`
        WHEN `an authorised surveyor` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 10(4): a person must not perform any survey or engage in survey work unless (a) a registered surveyor with a practising
-- certificate, (b) an authorised surveyor, or (c) "under the direction or supervision of" one of them.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Who, `under the direction or supervision of a qualified surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may perform survey work` IF
        `may certify a survey` `the person`
    OR  `under the direction or supervision of a qualified surveyor`

-- s 10(2): a person must not use "RS" before the name, or titles likely to make anyone believe the person is "authorised to supply
-- survey services in Singapore", or hold out as such, "unless at the time of so doing the person is a registered surveyor who has in
-- force a practising certificate, or is a licensed corporation, a licensed partnership, a licensed limited liability partnership or
-- a partnership consisting wholly of registered surveyors". An authorised surveyor is NOT in this list.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Who
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may hold out as authorised to supply survey services` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a registered surveyor with a practising certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership wholly of registered surveyors` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 10(3): no one may "recover in any court any charge, fee or remuneration for any survey services" unless the one rendering them is
-- (a) a registered surveyor with a practising certificate acting "on the person's own account or as a partner in a licensed
-- partnership, a licensed limited liability partnership or a partnership consisting wholly of registered surveyors"; (b) an allied
-- professional "only by reason of being a partner in a licensed partnership or a licensed limited liability partnership"; or (c) "a
-- licensed corporation or a licensed limited liability partnership". (A licensed partnership as such is not in (c); its partners
-- sue under (a) or (b). An authorised surveyor is not listed at all.)
DECLARE Capacity IS ONE OF
    `on own account`
    `as a partner in a licensed partnership or LLP`
    `as a partner in a partnership wholly of registered surveyors`
    `as an employee`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Who, `the capacity` IS A Capacity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may recover fees in court` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a registered surveyor with a practising certificate` THEN
        CONSIDER `the capacity`
        WHEN `as an employee` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `an allied professional` THEN
        CONSIDER `the capacity`
        WHEN `as a partner in a licensed partnership or LLP` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a licensed corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10(5), 30(2), 34 -- offences`

-- s 10(5): contravening s 10(1), (2) or (4) -- fine not exceeding $10,000. s 10(3) is not in that list: suing for fees while
-- unqualified is simply unrecoverable, not an offence. s 30(2): without lawful excuse refusing to attend, answer truly or produce
-- documents to an Investigation Committee or the Board -- $5,000. s 34: wilful false entry in a register, or procuring a licence,
-- practising certificate or registration by false representation -- $10,000. No imprisonment is provided in any of them.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `certifying a survey without being qualified`
    `holding out as authorised to supply survey services`
    `performing survey work without being qualified or supervised`
    `suing for fees without being qualified`
    `refusing to give evidence to the Board`
    `falsifying a register`
    `procuring registration by a false declaration`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `suing for fees without being qualified` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `suing for fees without being qualified` THEN 0
    WHEN `refusing to give evidence to the Board` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 10000

§§ `12 -- registration`

-- s 12(1): every person "21 years of age and above" is, on payment of the prescribed fee, entitled to be registered if (a) he or she
-- satisfies the Board of one of three qualifying routes -- a certificate of competency, a recognised professional examination with
-- further examination and practical experience, or recognised training and examination -- AND (b) "has passed a professional
-- interview conducted by the Board". (2): "Despite subsection (1), the Board may refuse to register any person who is not, in the
-- opinion of the Board, of good character and reputation."
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `has a qualifying route under s 12(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passed the professional interview` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of good character and reputation in the Board's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be registered` IF
        `the applicant`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the applicant`'s `has a qualifying route under s 12(1)(a)`
    AND `the applicant`'s `passed the professional interview`
    AND `the applicant`'s `paid the prescribed fee`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may refuse registration` IF
        (NOT `entitled to be registered` `the applicant`)
    OR  (NOT `the applicant`'s `of good character and reputation in the Board's opinion`)

§§ `15 -- the practising certificate year`

-- s 15(1): a registered surveyor who wants to do survey work "after 31 December of any year" must apply "not later than 1 December of
-- that year" for a certificate for "the succeeding year". (2): a first application after registration "may be made at any time during
-- the year" and the certificate may be issued "for the remainder of the year". (5): one who misses the s 15(1) deadline may, on an
-- additional fee, get a certificate for (a) the succeeding year if applying "during the month of December", or (b) the remainder of
-- the year if applying "on or after 1 January". (6): a certificate is in force until 31 December of its year.
--
-- Encoded: an application dated `month`/`day`. `holds this year's certificate` distinguishes the renewing surveyor (applying for next
-- year) from one who lapsed (and so missed the previous 1 December). Read: a lapsed, non-first-time applicant falls under s 15(5)(b).
DECLARE Period IS ONE OF
    `the succeeding year`
    `the remainder of this year`

GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before 1 December` IF
        `month` LESS THAN 12
    OR  (`month` EQUALS 12 AND `day` EQUALS 1)

GIVEN `first application after registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds this year's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Period
`the certificate period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `first application after registration`) AND `holds this year's certificate`
    THEN `the succeeding year`
    ELSE `the remainder of this year`

GIVEN `first application after registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds this year's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an additional fee is payable` IF
        (NOT `first application after registration`)
    AND (    (NOT `holds this year's certificate`)
         OR  (NOT `is on or before 1 December` `month` `day`))

-- s 15(8): a change of practice address "must be notified ... to the Registrar within 2 weeks of the change".
GIVEN `days after the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the address change was notified in time` IF `days after the change` AT MOST 14

§§ `17(1), (9) -- licensing a limited corporation`

-- s 17(1): the Board may license a limited corporation if (a) its memorandum makes supplying survey services "a primary object";
-- (b) "it has a paid-up capital of at least $1 million"; (c) its articles require "a prescribed number or proportion of the
-- directors" to be registered surveyors or allied professionals with practising certificates; (d) its survey business is under the
-- control of a director who is a registered surveyor with a practising certificate, authorised by board resolution to make all final
-- survey decisions; and (e) it is insured under s 21. (9): the prescribed proportion is "a majority of the directors" unless the
-- Minister gazettes another. (Encoded with the default majority only.) (6): the Board may still refuse on past conduct.
DECLARE Corporation HAS
    `survey services are a primary object` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid-up capital` IS A NUMBER
    `directors` IS A NUMBER
    `qualified directors` IS A NUMBER
    `has a controlling surveyor director authorised by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is insured under s 21` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a majority of directors are qualified` IF
    `the corporation`'s `qualified directors` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the corporation`'s `directors`

GIVEN `the corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may license the limited corporation` IF
        `the corporation`'s `survey services are a primary object`
    AND `the corporation`'s `paid-up capital` AT LEAST 1000000
    AND `a majority of directors are qualified` `the corporation`
    AND `the corporation`'s `has a controlling surveyor director authorised by resolution`
    AND `the corporation`'s `is insured under s 21`

-- s 19(1)-(3): a licensed corporation, partnership or LLP must, "within 30 days of the occurrence" of a change in its board,
-- members, shareholders or partners (or of its constitution or the controlling resolution), give the Board "a true written report".
GIVEN `days after the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change was reported in time` IF `days after the change` AT MOST 30

§§ `25, 26(6), 27(2), 29 -- discipline`

-- s 25(1): the Board may cancel registration or "suspend him or her from practice for a period not exceeding 12 months" on grounds
-- (a)-(k). (2): where no cause of sufficient gravity exists, "a penalty not exceeding $20,000", censure, or the cost of correcting a
-- cadastral survey. (3): only after "an opportunity of being heard either personally or by counsel" and "a hearing at which at least
-- 3 members of the Board are present". s 27(2): for a licensed firm the penalty is "not exceeding $50,000".
DECLARE Respondent IS ONE OF
    `a registered surveyor`
    `a licensed firm`

GIVEN `the respondent` IS A Respondent
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum Board penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the respondent`
    WHEN `a registered surveyor` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a licensed firm` THEN 50000

GIVEN `a ground in s 25(1) exists` IS A BOOLEAN, `was given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN, `Board members present at the hearing` IS A NUMBER, `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may suspend for that period` IF
        `a ground in s 25(1) exists`
    AND `was given an opportunity to be heard`
    AND `Board members present at the hearing` AT LEAST 3
    AND `months of suspension` AT MOST 12

-- s 25(6) (and s 27(5) for licences): an order "does not take effect until the expiry of 30 days after the Board has informed the
-- person concerned"; if within that period notice of appeal is given, it does not take effect "unless the order is confirmed ... or
-- the appeal is for any reason dismissed".
GIVEN `days since informed` IS A NUMBER, `appealed within 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `confirmed or dismissed on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has taken effect` IF
        `days since informed` GREATER THAN 30
    AND (    (NOT `appealed within 30 days`)
         OR  `confirmed or dismissed on appeal`)

-- s 25(7): for ground (g), a surveyor is "not to be deemed to have taken reasonable steps" to stop a firm's misconduct "unless he or
-- she satisfies the Board" that (a) it was done without his or her knowledge, (b) he or she could not influence the firm, or (c)
-- being able to, he or she "exercised all due diligence". The burden is on the surveyor.
GIVEN `satisfied the Board it was without knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the Board of no influence` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the Board of due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surveyor took reasonable steps` IF
        `satisfied the Board it was without knowledge`
    OR  `satisfied the Board of no influence`
    OR  `satisfied the Board of due diligence`

-- s 26(2)-(6): a registered surveyor may apply to have his or her name removed, by affidavit served "at least 2 months before the
-- application is heard"; but "No order is to be made" if (a) "disciplinary action is pending" or (b) the conduct is under inquiry or
-- investigation by an Investigation Committee.
GIVEN `affidavit served at least 2 months before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN, `disciplinary action pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `under investigation by an Investigation Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may remove the name on request` IF
        `affidavit served at least 2 months before the hearing`
    AND (NOT `disciplinary action pending`)
    AND (NOT `under investigation by an Investigation Committee`)

-- s 29: the Board may, "after the expiry of at least one year from the cancellation of registration", consider a fresh application.
GIVEN `months since cancellation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may consider re-registration` IF `months since cancellation` AT LEAST 12

§§ `15(10), 16(3), 17(8), 18(4), 28 -- appeals`

-- Refusal or cancellation of a practising certificate (ss 15(10), 16(3)) and cancellation, suspension, revocation or a pecuniary
-- penalty (s 28) go to "the General Division of the High Court whose decision is final", within 30 days. Refusal of a licence
-- (s 17(8)) goes to "the Minister whose decision is final", within 30 days. Licence conditions (s 18(4)) go to the Minister "in the
-- prescribed manner" -- no period is stated in the Act.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal of a practising certificate`
    `cancellation of a practising certificate`
    `refusal of a licence`
    `conditions on a licence`
    `cancellation of registration or suspension`
    `revocation of a licence`
    `a pecuniary penalty`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `the Minister`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal of a licence` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `conditions on a licence` THEN `the Minister`
    OTHERWISE `the General Division of the High Court`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act fixes a 30-day appeal period` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `conditions on a licence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
